WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
A ripple spreads across a still pond.

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.980
Two corks float on it.

3
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.080
The ripple travels on,
but the water doesn't:

4
00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.200
each cork just bobs up and down in place.

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.880
Between the corks lies
exactly half a wavelength.

6
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.290
As the ripple passes, how do the
two corks' movements compare?

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.930
In this mission, you'll measure phase:
how far through its cycle each point on

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.020
a wave is, in degrees or in radians.

9
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.000
Then you'll line up two
traces on one graph,

10
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.230
and work out which one
leads, and by how much.

11
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.950
Your mission: predict how the
two corks' movements compare,

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.270
and explain why.
